{"step_index":220,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:20:36Z","input_tokens":2592,"cache_read_tokens":181193,"output_tokens":1139,"thinking":"The problem is mismatched data between the uploaded document and the displayed digitized output. The current display shows unrelated, hardcoded items instead of reflecting the uploaded invoice data. The goal is to correct this mismatch without modifying the core features.\n\n\nThe mismatch stems from the code's fallback mechanism. When an API key is missing or invalid, the system defaults to hardcoded items in `simulateLocalExtraction`, which bypasses real data extraction and creates the discrepancy. This function is returning the static items when the Gemini API is unavailable. The issue needs to be corrected by ensuring accurate extraction or a proper error handling in the fallback scenario.\n\n\nReal-time OCR extraction is feasible using Tesseract.js directly in the browser, eliminating server dependencies for image and PDF processing. This will parse uploaded documents for key invoice details like vendor, invoice number, date, items, quantities, rates, and totals. A progress indicator will show during OCR processing.\n\nNext, I need to figure out how to integrate this in the UI.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"echo \"GEMINI_API_KEY is: ${GEMINI_API_KEY:-empty}\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Check if GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable is set"}}]}
