{"step_index":222,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:20:50Z","input_tokens":2750,"cache_read_tokens":182269,"output_tokens":2023,"thinking":"The absence of the API key suggests a local, browser-based execution scenario without proper key configuration, potentially explaining the data mismatch. The user is observing a discrepancy where the processed output incorrectly displays unrelated items compared to the original invoice.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe current implementation uses hardcoded static items, thus always displaying irrelevant data regardless of the uploaded invoice. The immediate need is to enable actual extraction from the uploaded documents. The initial approach involves client-side OCR (Tesseract.js) to convert images into text, then parsing this recognized text to identify key invoice elements like vendor name, GSTIN, invoice number, and date using regular expressions.\n\n\nParsing extracted text to locate invoice details necessitates specific regular expressions. Identified requirements include patterns for date formats, table line items (description, quantity, rate, amount), subtotals, taxes, and bank details. If direct text extraction fails, an interactive review mechanism is needed, showing raw extracted text and enabling real-time edits synced to the output, also handling unreadable fields gracefully.\n\n\nAdding Tesseract.js and PDF.js to the `index.html` file enables client-side OCR and PDF text extraction functionalities. The browser will then have access to these libraries through `window.Tesseract` and `window.pdfjsLib` objects. A dedicated `invoiceTextParser.js` module will be built to extract relevant data from the raw text.\n\nThe parser will extract vendor name, GSTIN, invoice number, and date using regular expressions. It will identify and parse invoice line items using patterns associated with the description, quantity, rate, and amount, specifically looking for numerical data from right to left in the lines. Different line item formats require consideration of diverse layouts.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":45,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/index.h